I thought this was possible, but in fact, I did not find a way to do
that either. However, perhaps what you actually want is a preview of
the plot generated by the current script? In that case, activate the
script window, and select Preview->Plot Preview from the toolbar.

(Some enhancements to that will also be in the next release).

> Also, where can I find the "environment" window/tab? The one in
> RStudio that lists variables and data frames you have in your current
> project.

It's called "Workspace" in RKWard, default placement is top of the left
sidebar.

Regards
Thomas
